schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Millions of Bitcoin have been permanently lost to forgotten passwords and lost seed phrases
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Estimates suggest that millions of Bitcoin, worth billions of dollars,
    have been permanently lost due to forgotten passwords, lost seed phrases,
    and deceased owners with no succession plan." (recovery-planning.md, "Why
    Recovery Planning Matters")
  evidence: >-
    No specific study or named estimate (e.g. Chainalysis-style lost-coin
    research) is cited in the article body. Article frontmatter lists
    `sources: []` — no supporting citation attached.
  source_lineage: "src/content/docs/recovery-planning.md (frontmatter sources field is empty)"
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the opening justification for why recovery planning is
    "essential" rather than merely advisable, framing the entire article's
    stakes.
  uncertainty: >-
    "Millions of Bitcoin" is directionally consistent with widely-circulated
    third-party lost-coin estimates (e.g. Chainalysis-style research often
    cited elsewhere in the industry, commonly landing in the 3-4 million BTC
    range), but no such source is named or linked in this article, and the
    article's own `sources: []` field confirms nothing was attached. Treat the
    magnitude as directionally plausible but unverified from this source
    alone.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/recovery-planning.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
